<title>USA: Commercial Metals Q2 shr $0.47 vs $0.67.</title>
<headline>Commercial Metals Q2 shr $0.47 vs $0.67.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>COMMERCIAL METALS COMPANY</p>
<p>			CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF EARNINGS</p>
<p>			  (in thousands except share data)</p>
<p>			   Three months ended   Six months ended</p>
<p>		     2/28/97	2/29/96     2/28/97     2/29/96</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>   Total	    525,755     518,181   1,056,716   1,108,400</p>
<p> Net Earnings a     7,201	10,010	16,378	20,842</p>
<p> Net earnings/shr    0.47	  0.67	  1.06	  1.36</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>outstanding  15,413,273  15,025,543  15,400,735  15,298,581</p>
<p>Note a :The LIFO method of inventory valuation had the effect of decreasing net earnings for the quarter $497,000, $0.03 per share compared to an increase in net earnings of $722,000, or $0.05 per share last year and for the six months net earnings were $149,000 lower ($0.01 per share) compared to an increase of $868,000 ($0.06 per share) last year.</p>
